course: dictionary
lesson: 5878
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the words around it. This is context, and it is the best clue you have. The word mango has two meanings: a fruit, and the tree that the fruit grows on.
explain: «Farmers in Australia and Africa still use them on mango and cashew trees.» The word trees tells you that mango here means the tree, not the fruit. You cannot put ants on a fruit in the same way, so the clue is in the sentence.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If "the fruit" makes sense, use that. If "the tree" fits better, use that one instead. Always check.
fact: A mango is a sweet, juicy tropical fruit with orange flesh.
fact: A mango has a smooth skin and a large flat stone inside.
fact: Mango can also mean the tree that the fruit grows on.
fact: Mangoes grow in places such as India, Pakistan, the Caribbean and northern Australia.
fact: Mango is a noun. Its plural is mangoes, or mangos.
exercise: «Farmers in Australia and Africa still use them on mango and cashew trees.» In this sentence, what does mango mean? | *The tree that the fruit grows on | A sweet, juicy fruit | A large flat stone | A kind of ant
exercise: Jade ate a ripe mango with her lunch. What is a mango in this sentence? | A loud noise | *A sweet, juicy fruit | A small, sharp tool | The tree it grows on
exercise: Which spelling is the correct plural of mango? | mango's | mangies | *mangoes | mangoe
test: Where do mangoes grow, according to the lessons? | Greenland | *India | Antarctica | Iceland
test: What is inside a mango? | Hard bones | *A large flat stone | Seeds only | A small green leaf
exam: «He sliced the mango and shared it between the four children.» Which meaning of mango is used here? | The tree | A kind of ant | *The fruit | A school subject
